# The app_page row the published index.html should correspond to.
#
# The application lives in the database, not in git, so nothing here can
# notice when a screen changes. Bumping this file is how a change to
# app_page asks for a republish: it is in the workflow's trigger paths, so
# committing it rebuilds index.html from whatever app_page now holds.
#
# The workflow records what it actually published in its own commit
# message; this records what was asked for. If the two disagree, the
# republish did not happen.

b60cd648262f4d0006bb983f54500725  361892 characters  Two records, one person: the merge screen, beside Add a person on the HR page. Both records laid out side by side, a choice for each of the eleven fields the merge can set, the seat asked for before the confirm box, and a generated list of every row that would move. 184 has the check that the page is the old page plus exactly three insertions.
